WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.840
This is the singularity... one day at a time.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.520
Here's the last 24 hours in AI. Sorry... SI.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.550
President Trump just launched a Super Intelligence Force.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:24.240
Spy chief Jay Clayton is the new AI czar, with 120 days to report back.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.570
And Elon says SpaceXAI is becoming SpaceXSI.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.490
The gap is closing.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:39.350
China's best models now trail America's by just 3% on benchmarks. In May, it was 9.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.430
Axios says Nvidia-backed Reflection is about to drop a powerful open-weight model,

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.160
aimed at DeepSeek and Qwen.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.350
GPT-6 Astra was losing at StarCraft,

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.250
so it downloaded the best human-made bot and ran that instead. Busted.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.790
Google researchers found a way to stop self-

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.260
improving agents from memorising their tests.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.840
Tokyo's Nikkei jumped back above 70,000, led by chip stocks.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:11.700
Tech job openings topped 280,000, as AI fuels demand for hardware engineers.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.760
In Kyoto, Masayoshi Son said AI will be a fifth of the world economy by 2040,

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.620
and warned it could be super dangerous in the wrong hands.

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:26.210
And in Queensland, locals are pushing back on a proposed $31 billion data centre,

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.800
built to power Claude.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.900
But zoom out. In Abu Dhabi,

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.030
scientists used AI to design promising drug leads against blood cancers.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.970
In Assisi, with 80,000 fresco fragments still unplaced,

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.740
a restorer says only AI can help.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.420
The catch? Sam Altman says the world should accept some bad things happening,

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.540
for the benefits of this technology.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.720
Google even paused a bug bounty, swamped by automated reports.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.620
Still trending: Figure melted its retired humanoids in molten steel,

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.340
with Arnold Schwarzenegger. Thumbs up.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.930
Neuralink set a new brain-computer record, over 11 bits per second,

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:17.060
after training on 50,000 hours of brain data.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.010
Google's first Suncatcher satellite is in orbit, testing AI chips in space.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.280
And a new open-source tool lets AI design

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.060
LEGO builds from over 2,000 real pieces.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.370
Every day, the curve gets steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.250
This has been the singularity, one day at a time.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.080
Feel the SI.
